            <fr:title text="A mesh axis may appear only once">A mesh axis may appear only once</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1786546736336</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p><fr:link href="/XGI0/" title="Sharding" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/XGI0/" display-uri="XGI0" type="local">Sharded</fr:link> matmul, case 4: both multiplicands have a <html:em>non-contracting</html:em> dimension sharded along the same mesh axis, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A[I_X, J] \cdot  B[J, K_X]]]></fr:tex>. Why is this invalid, and how do you resolve it?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  A mesh axis may appear <html:strong>at most once</html:strong> in a sharding. Writing <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C[I_X, K_X]]]></fr:tex> would give shard <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i]]></fr:tex> only the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(i,i)]]></fr:tex> block — the block diagonal. The off-diagonal blocks of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C]]></fr:tex> exist nowhere, so the result is unrecoverable.

  <html:strong>The fix</html:strong> is to <fr:link href="/VSDZ/" title="AllGather" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/VSDZ/" display-uri="VSDZ" type="local">AllGather</fr:link> one of the two inputs along <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex> first, so that <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex> appears once in the output:

  <html:ul><html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {AllGather}_X(A) \to  A[I, J]]]></fr:tex>, giving <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C[I, K_X]]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {AllGather}_X(B) \to  B[J, K]]]></fr:tex>, giving <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C[I_X, K]]]></fr:tex>.</html:li></html:ul>

  Which one you pick is decided by the sharding the downstream ops want.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
