            <fr:route>/KIRV/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Matching contracting shards give partial sums">Matching contracting shards give partial sums</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1786546736136</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p><fr:link href="/XGI0/" title="Sharding" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/XGI0/" display-uri="XGI0" type="local">Sharded</fr:link> matmul, case 3: both multiplicands are sharded along the contracting dimension on the same mesh axis, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A[I, J_X] \cdot  B[J_X, K]]]></fr:tex>. What happens, and which primitive fixes it?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  The local shards <html:em>can</html:em> be multiplied — they share contracting indices — but each device ends up with only a <html:strong>partial sum</html:strong>, written <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C[I, K]\{U_X\}]]></fr:tex>, "unreduced along <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex>":

  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[A \cdot  B = \sum _i A[:,i] \otimes  B[i,:]]]></fr:tex>

  Device <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i]]></fr:tex> owns the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i]]></fr:tex>-th column block of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> and the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i]]></fr:tex>-th row block of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>, so it computes exactly the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i]]></fr:tex>-th term of that sum.

  <html:strong>The fix</html:strong> is <fr:link href="/U351/" title="AllReduce" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/U351/" display-uri="U351" type="local">AllReduce</fr:link> along <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex> for a replicated <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C[I, K]]]></fr:tex> — or the cheaper <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {ReduceScatter}_{X,K} \to  C[I, K_X]]]></fr:tex> if you can leave the output sharded. That is <fr:link href="/MJ7A/" title="AllReduce is two collectives, not one" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/MJ7A/" display-uri="MJ7A" type="local">half the cost</fr:link>, and defers the gather, possibly forever.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
